  "description": "The 2026 election for Tennessee's 2nd Congressional District features incumbent Republican Tim Burchett, who has held the seat since 2019, facing Democratic challenger Michaela Barnett and two independent candidates. The district, anchored by Knoxville, was redrawn in May 2026 under a new mid-decade congressional map passed by Tennessee's Republican-controlled legislature, which has been challenged in court by Democrats as racially gerrymandered. Burchett has won re-election with over 69% of the vote in recent cycles, and the race is rated 'Safe Republican' or 'Solid R' by all major nonpartisan forecasters. The primary election is scheduled for August 6, 2026, with the general election on November 3, 2026.",
